<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy | 88cutouts" description="How 88cutouts handles local composition tools, optional analytics, hosting logs, contact emails and cookie choices.">
  <div class="wrap"><article class="prose"><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>Last updated 26 September 2026.</p>
<p>88cutouts is operated by Sarath. Contact <a href="mailto:hello@88cutouts.com">hello@88cutouts.com</a> with privacy questions. The public site has no visitor accounts and does not require your name or email to download an asset.</p>
<h2>Browser tools</h2>
<p>Lettering and collage compositions are rendered in your browser. The site does not upload your generated image or the freeform text you enter into these tools. Saving or copying happens on your device. When you publish a result in another app, that app's privacy practices apply.</p>
<h2>Google Analytics</h2>
<p>Google Analytics 4 loads by default, unless you have turned it off in the site's cookie settings. It measures page visits and interactions such as downloads, copies, preset selections and the number of search results. Search query text is not sent by our search event code. Google may process device and browser information, approximate location and online identifiers, and sets analytics cookies such as <code>_ga</code>.</p>
<p>Online identifiers and usage information can be personal data. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/12017362">Google Analytics data collection information</a>. You can turn analytics off and still use the website.</p>
<h2>Your cookie choice</h2>
<p>We store your analytics preference in local storage under <code>88cutouts-analytics-v1</code>. This preference remains until you change it or clear your browser's site data. Use <button type="button" class="privacy-settings">Cookie settings</button> to change your choice. Turning analytics off disables further analytics collection through this page and attempts to remove the site's Google Analytics cookies. It does not erase information previously received by Google.</p>
<h2>Hosting and technical logs</h2>
<p>Cloudflare delivers and protects this website. Requests may include your IP address, browser details, requested URL and time of access. These are separate from optional analytics. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>. Fonts are served from this site.</p>
<h2>Contact emails</h2>
<p>If you email us, your address and the information you include are used to respond and investigate the request. Do not send passwords, payment information or private images that are unnecessary for resolving the issue. Ask through the same address if you want your correspondence deleted; some information may need to be retained to resolve a dispute or meet applicable obligations.</p>
<h2>Advertising</h2>
<p>The site intends to use Google AdSense, but this version does not load Google advertising scripts. If advertising is enabled, this policy and the consent interface must be updated for the actual setup before ads run. Analytics consent here is not advertising consent. Google and its advertising partners may use cookies and identifiers when ads are enabled; see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from partner sites</a>.</p>
<h2>Choices and enquiries</h2>
<p>You can turn off analytics, clear site data, block cookies, or contact us about access, correction or deletion requests. Rights depend on your location and circumstances. We do not sell personal data or operate a newsletter. The site is not directed at children under 13.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2><p>Changes to collection or consent will be reflected in this page's updated date. Contact us if a description here does not match what you observe.</p></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
